* Added ProviderStateChanged event to ProviderManager and adjust ProviderUpdated usage
* Removed unused ProviderUpdatedEventArgs and ProviderManagerChangedState

This PR includes the commit for #112 on `dev/7.1.0` as well as a few fixes to the samples to account for the change in usage of ProviderUpdated vs ProviderStateChanged.

THIS IS A BREAKING CHANGE.

Where previously you would see this to respond to changes in the provider:
```
ProviderManager.Instance.ProviderUpdated += OnProviderUpdated;

void OnProviderUpdated(object sender, ProviderUpdatedEventArgs args)
{
    if (args.Reason == ProviderManagerChangedState.ProviderUpdated)
    {
        // The global provider has been set.
    }

    if (args.Reason == ProviderManagerChangedState.ProviderStateChanged)
    {
        // The state of the global provider has changed.
    }
}
```

You must now handle these logical paths using separate events, instead of pivoting on the `Reason`. The new way is as follows:

```
ProviderManager.Instance.ProviderUpdated += OnProviderUpdated;
ProviderManager.Instance.ProviderStateChanged += OnProviderStateChanged;

void OnProviderUpdated(object sender, IProvider provider)
{
    // The global provider has been set.
}

void OnProviderStateChanged(object sender, ProviderStateChangedEventArgs args)
{
    // The state of the global provider has changed.
}
```

This PR replaces the local `ConfirmDialog` component, used by the `prompts` module, with the `ConfirmModal` component from the `frontend-shared` package and removes the then-unused `Dialog` and `ConfirmDialog` components, their tests and styles.

There are no user-facing changes for the vast majority of users. For users with browsers that no longer support `window.confirm` in third-party iframes, they will now see the consolidated version of the confirm-modal UI.

## To Test

* Check out this branch/`make dev`
* Edit `/src/shared/prompts.js` and comment out the following lines:

```
  const result = window.confirm(message);
  if (result || Date.now() - start >= 10) {
    return result;
  }
```
* On a test page in the local dev server, select some text and click `Annotate`.
* Select "Log Out" from the user menu

You should see:

