1. Currently the Verifier may be broken and seems to send garbage state roots to the fraud prover, which means that the fraud prover has no chance of detecting fraud. This _could_ be a simple misconfiguration/offset issue on my end, but, all i'm doing in this regard is to run the verifier with the standard command (`docker-compose up --scale verifier=1 --build --detach`) and then pointing the fraud-prover at 8547. Notably, a month or so ago, the Verifier was just fine... so not sure what has happened to it in the intervening 4 weeks.  

